One of the main challenges in this transition is ensuring grid stability. Renewable sources like solar and wind are intermittent, meaning they do not generate power consistently. To address this, PLN is investing in smart grid technology and large-scale energy storage solutions, like batteries and pumped-storage hydropower. Furthermore, the transition requires substantial financial investment, estimated to be in the hundreds of billions of dollars. Securing this funding through international partnerships and green financing mechanisms is a key priority for the government and PLN.

