To counter these risks, energy companies are investing heavily in advanced cybersecurity measures. These include developing robust defense systems, conducting regular security audits, and training employees to recognize and respond to phishing attempts and other social engineering tactics. Collaboration between government agencies and private sector companies is also crucial to share threat intelligence and coordinate a unified defense against sophisticated cyber adversaries.

[Pertanyaan]: According to the passage, what makes power grids more susceptible to cyber threats?','[{"key": "A", "text": "Their reliance on outdated technology."}, {"key": "B", "text": "A lack of trained personnel."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Their interconnection with smart technologies."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Insufficient government funding."}]'::jsonb,'C','Paragraf pertama menyatakan, "...power grids, which are now interconnected with smart technologies, are more vulnerable...".','BI',14);
