  INSERT INTO public.questions (package_id,content,options,correct_answer,explanation,category,order_index) VALUES (pkg_id,'[Teks Bacaan]:
Effective leadership in a technical environment requires a unique blend of skills. While technical expertise is fundamental, it is not sufficient on its own. A successful leader in a field like engineering must also be adept at communication, team motivation, and strategic planning. They need to be able to translate complex technical concepts into understandable terms for stakeholders who may not have a technical background.

Furthermore, a great leader fosters an environment of innovation and continuous improvement. This involves encouraging team members to experiment with new ideas, even if it means accepting occasional failures as learning opportunities. By empowering their team and providing clear direction, leaders can guide their departments through complex projects and drive the organization toward its long-term goals. This balanced approach is what separates a competent manager from a truly inspiring leader.

